      "writtenOn": "2019-11-13T08:24:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand your comment. \n\n\u003e\u003e I believe that it isn\u0027t the responsibility of the muxer module to check for available disk space. \n\nThis is a kind of workaround. Currently file write does not return any error, so user may get corrupted file if storage is almost full. We checked if we can protect from user in write. But it\u0027s difficult to add error handling on every write operation. With this check, current behavior can be improved, we think.\n\n\u003e\u003e But if we are going with this logic in SDK, we need to do this at the NDK level as well, I mean in NdkMediaMuxer.cpp\n\nWe considered to do it, but currently storage manager is in Java layer. We could not find other way to get it from native layer.",
      "parentUuid": "04c15dba_de5ad6bd",
      "revId": "1ea30440ef177ad1c8839b2ae67ec393cfbd830a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
